           description: <short summary derived from the AC description>\n                  service: \"\"\n                  path: <see below>\n                  last_updated: \"<today, YYYY-MM-DD>\"\n                  user_stories:\n                    - story: <story file path from subject>\n                      scenario_id: <lineage id from subject>\n                      merge_date: \"<today, YYYY-MM-DD>\"\n                  merged_steps:\n                    given: <verbatim from the AC's steps.given>\n                    when:  <verbatim from the AC's steps.when>\n                    then:  <verbatim from the AC's steps.then>\n            3. `path:` names the generated test file this scenario's Go\n               test is written into. REUSE an existing `path:` from a\n               scenario of the same command or feature family — several\n               scenarios share one file on purpose, so related\n               behaviours are read together. Invent a new one only when\n               no existing file fits, and then make it\n               `<suite path>/<family>_test.go`, where <suite path> is\n               the `path:` of the architecture.testing.suites[] entry\n               whose `service:` matches this scenario's.\n            4. Preserve existing file ordering and indentation. Do not\n               touch any other entry.\n\n      - Q: |\n          Does the registry contain duplicate entries for this acceptance\n          criterion?\n\n          Two entries are duplicates when both reference the subject's\n          lineage scenario id in their `user_stories[]` list, OR their\n          `merged_steps` describe the same observable behavior with the\n          same service.\n\n          Pass when exactly one entry references this AC.\n          Fail when two or more entries reference it.\n\n          Context: emit one line per matching entry, then a verdict.\n            - \"match: <scenario id> — '<short description>'\"\n            - \"Verdict: unique / duplicate (<N> entries)\"\n        rationale: \"Each AC must map to a single registry entry; duplicates pollute the registry and break lineage.\"\n        F: |\n          Collapse the duplicate entries into a single one.\n\n          Use the Edit tool against the registry file referenced by the\n          subject. Steps:\n            1. Choose a winning entry (prefer the lower-numbered id; prefer\n               `INT-` over `E2E-` when both layers cover the same behavior\n               and an integration test exists).\n            2. Move every `user_stories[]` item from the losing entry into\n               the winner's `user_stories[]`, preserving order and\n               deduplicating by `(story, scenario_id)`.\n            3. Union the `merged_steps` so every step from both entries\n               appears in the winner, deduplicated.\n            4. Delete the losing entry. Do not renumber other ids.\n","numLines":102,"startLine":1,"totalLines":102}}}
